      "kind": "text",
      "text": "This lesson is optional. It helps you read harmony, but you do not need it to complete Grade 5, and nothing in it is in the Grade 5 assessment."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "A common progression is a second-inversion tonic chord (Ic) followed by the dominant chord in root position (V). Both chords have the dominant note in the bass. It is called a six-four five-three, because the first chord has a 6th and a 4th above its bass, and the second a 5th and a 3rd."
    },
